{
 "format": "pcbpro",
 "version": 1,
 "name": "Plexi crunch 50W",
 "author": "",
 "revision": "A",
 "notes": "Plexi crunch 50W\nCrunch: breaks up early; roll your guitar's volume back to clean up.\n\nOutput: 2 x EL34, push-pull class AB, fixed bias, adjustable\nOutput power: about 50 W clean into 8 ohm\nB+ / plate: 460 V at the OT, about 460 V plate to cathode\nIdle current: 36 mA per tube (bias about -38 V)\nPlate dissipation: 14.9 W per tube = 60% of the 25 W rating\nBias adjust range: -24 V to -48 V (fail-safe: an open trimmer gives maximum negative bias)\nPresence: up to +7 dB at 4 kHz (in the power amp, after the distortion)\n\nWhere it distorts (gain on 10): V1B does most of the distorting.\n  V1A: clean\n  V1B: clips, +29 dB\nHiss with the gain on 10: about -78 dB below the playing level (-98 dB with the gain at noon)\n\nPower transformer: 345-0-345 VAC at 241 mA DC, 6.3 V 4.7 A, bias tap about 45 VAC; 230 V primary, about 154 VA\nOutput transformer: 3.4k plate-to-plate to 8 ohm, 65 W or more\nFilter choke: 5-10 H, 30 mA or more\nMains fuse: T1.25 A slow-blow (230 V), plus a power switch\nTubes: 3 x 12AX7, 2 x EL34\nRectifier: 4 x 1N4007 on the board (solid state)\nSpeaker: 8 ohm, 75 W or more\nChassis parts: 1/4\" speaker jack, power and (optional) standby switches, mains inlet, pilot lamp, knobs\n\n- The heaters are elevated to about +52 V: the cathode follower's cathode sits near 200 V, and this keeps the heater-to-cathode voltage inside the 12AX7's rating (and lowers hum).\n- The 2 EL34s draw 3.0 A of heater current: run twisted pairs from the 6.3 V winding to each power tube's H1/H2 pads (or daisy-chain the pads) instead of wide board traces; the preamp tubes' heaters stay on the board.\n- Before the first power-up turn the BIAS trimmer for the most negative bias, then set it for about 32 mA per tube: 32 mV across each 1R cathode resistor (pads K1-K2).\n- If the amp squeals or motorboats when you turn it up, the feedback is positive: swap the two output-transformer secondary leads (SPK / COM).\n- Solid-state rectification gives a tight, punchy response with full B+ at switch-on; the filter caps are rated for the no-load voltage.\n- Mains wiring (inlet, fuse, switch, transformer primary) stays on the chassis. The board carries lethal voltages: the bleeder drains the caps in about a minute - always measure B+ before touching anything.\n\nFirst power-up:\n1. Check every electrolytic's polarity, the heater wiring and the mains wiring before the first switch-on, and bring the amp up through a dim-bulb tester or a variac.\n2. With no tubes fitted the heaters should read 6.3 VAC at the sockets and B+ will sit high (about 487 V): the filter caps are rated for it.\n3. Always connect a speaker (or a load resistor) before playing: an unloaded output transformer can arc and destroy the power tubes or itself.\n4. Fit the tubes with the BIAS trimmer at maximum negative bias, then set 32 mA per tube (32 mV across each 1R).\n5. Measure the B+ nodes and the tube pins against the tables below: within 10-15 % means the amp is healthy.\n\nVoltage chart (DC to ground at idle):\nV1 12AX7: 1 PA 170 V, 2 GA 0.0 V, 3 KA 1.0 V, 4 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 5 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 6 PB 170 V, 7 GB 0.0 V, 8 KB 1.0 V, 9 HCT 6.3 VAC on +52 V\nV2 12AX7: 1 PA 316 V, 2 GA 170 V, 3 KA 172 V, 4 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 5 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 7 GB 0.0 V, 8 KB 0.0 V, 9 HCT 6.3 VAC on +52 V\nV3 12AX7: 1 PA 307 V, 2 GA 24 V, 3 KA 25 V, 4 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 5 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 6 PB 286 V, 7 GB 24 V, 8 KB 25 V, 9 HCT 6.3 VAC on +52 V\nV4 EL34: 1 G3 0.0 V, 2 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 3 A 455 V, 4 G2 456 V, 5 G1 -38 V, 7 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 8 K 0.0 V\nV5 EL34: 1 G3 0.0 V, 2 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 3 A 455 V, 4 G2 456 V, 5 G1 -38 V, 7 H 6.3 VAC on +52 V, 8 K 0.0 V",
